{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdKTKMBDx3T14kLw1mkBP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The WI-276 rework is complete. Final commit `a99efd3` carries the required `WI:` / `Train:` / `Base:` trailers, working tree is clean.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Rework finding addressed** (REVIEW-A MAJOR, `check_dupes.py:74`): `fingerprint()` hashed only the first `--min-tokens` window plus the block's total extent, so a duplicate whose opening 30 tokens and overall length were unchanged reused the stale census fingerprint and stayed silently exempt.\n\n**What I found:** a prior session in this worktree had already applied the fix to the staged working tree but never committed it. I verified, hardened, and committed it:\n\n1. **The fix (`check_dupes.py`)** — `fingerprint(block)` now hashes the block's **complete** normalized `(kind, text)` token signature via a new `_merged_signature(run)` helper that reconstructs the full merged block from its overlapping step‑1 windows (first window in full, then each subsequent window's one new trailing token). Any interior/trailing edit now rotates the fingerprint and drops the exemption. Still line‑number‑free.\n\n2. **The required CLI regression test** — `test_post_window_token_change_defeats_stale_fingerprint`: censuses a ~70‑token block, changes one token *past* the first window in both files while keeping the extent, and requires exit 1. I **proved it catches the bug** by running it against HEAD's buggy `fingerprint(window, length)` — it exits 0 (\"no duplicate blocks\") and the test fails there; on the fixed code it passes.\n\n3. **Census regenerated** (`docs/dupes-allow`) — all 226 fingerprints rotate under the new algorithm; exact multiset bijection with `--emit-census`; the dupes gate passes on the repo's own source.\n\n4. **Spine + derived artifacts** — LLR‑036 detail updated (\"a hash of its complete token signature\"); the arch MODULE MAP, OKF LLR‑036, and PROJECT_STATE.html regenerated deterministically so all G3 freshness gates stay green (the integrator re‑regenerates on the composed tree).\n\n**Verification (main‑repo `.venv`, Python 3.11.9):** `ruff format --check` and `ruff check` clean; `check_dupes` suite 14/14; full suite `1379 passed, 5 skipped, 1 failed`; every G3 freshness/integrity gate (arch‑map, okf, status‑map, trajectory‑map, derived‑gate, registry‑integrity) PASS.\n\n**One pre‑existing failure, out of scope:** `test_forward_only_unit_over_the_real_meta_repo` — `WI-275` is `done` in `work-items.csv` but its id still lives in `docs/status.md` (forward‑only), inherited from integration base `747f152`. Both files are integrator‑owned root coordination truth I'm forbidden to edit; neither is in my diff. The original build `3e1856d` documented this same condition, and the integrator scrubs `status.md` on the composed tree."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1876,"cache_read_input_tokens":115387,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1876},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1dcaf5b4-294e-4c8d-b277-991fa7c96d87","uuid":"32e70ef1-bea9-4efd-acc9-76f9942650b0","request_id":"req_011CdKTKJfQvVSq6NsxJRfF3"}
